{
  "formatVersion": 2,
  "title": "Room-by-room heating control",
  "description": "Two rooms are heated. In the living room, a PI thermostat sends a DPT 5.001 control value to a heating actuator, which drives a thermoelectric valve with PWM. The bedroom uses two-point (one-bit) control through a switching actuator. Open the living-room window in the Rooms panel: the contact switches the thermostat to frost protection. Write central mode 3/2/0 (DPT 20.102) from the USB interface panel; the thermostat Presence key restores comfort mode.",
